From bb8afdd6fdd522e8a0ccc4811997624fbbfca003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:56:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0325 -- emit raw stationary counts beside
 the ratio

stationary_frac is a within-block ratio. Both its counters increment in
Game::tick, so the quantity is game logic and reproducible from a TAS
reel. But the BLOCK BOUNDARY is per-100-flips, and the flip:tick ratio is
hardware-dependent -- so the number of ticks a block spans is too.

The same reel, same counters, same build:

    Gateway    ~18 blocks over ~5140 ticks   ~285 ticks/block   mean 0.11
    DOSBox-X  ~505 blocks over ~5140 ticks    ~10 ticks/block   mean 0.004

Neither is wrong. They are different statistics wearing one name. The
distribution is bimodal -- almost every block exactly 0.00, rare blocks
at 1.00 -- so a single fully-stationary block contributes 1/18 to one
mean and 1/505 to the other. A mean of block ratios is not comparable
across machines and should not have been quoted as though it were.

Emitting the raw counts lets them be summed across blocks into a pooled
stationary fraction, which is comparable. The ratio stays, because it is
still the right per-block view for spotting where stillness occurs.

This is load-bearing rather than tidy. The tilemap cache breaks even near
a 63% hit rate, hit rate tracks camera stillness, and the cache reaches
30.15 fps at a perfect hit rate -- so whether the measured reel resembles
real play is the difference between recording that lever as catastrophic
and recording it as the largest win available. That question cannot be
asked with a statistic that changes with the machine it was measured on.

Emit-only. No counter semantics change and no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index 2cee0637..01f53b0f 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -3408,7 +3408,7 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
     const double _stationary_frac = (NXE::Diag::g_w237_total_frames_block > 0)
         ? (double)NXE::Diag::g_w237_stationary_frames_block / (double)NXE::Diag::g_w237_total_frames_block
         : 0.0;
-    LOG_INFO("[mds-tilemap-cache n={} bg_h={} bg_m={} bg_state={} bg_t={} fg_h={} fg_m={} fg_state={} fg_t={} bg_ms_h={:.2f} bg_ms_m={:.2f} fg_ms_h={:.2f} fg_ms_m={:.2f} stationary_frac={:.2f}]",
+    LOG_INFO("[mds-tilemap-cache n={} bg_h={} bg_m={} bg_state={} bg_t={} fg_h={} fg_m={} fg_state={} fg_t={} bg_ms_h={:.2f} bg_ms_m={:.2f} fg_ms_h={:.2f} fg_ms_m={:.2f} stationary_frac={:.2f} stat_ticks={} tick_frames={}]",
              g_tilemap_cache_n_block,
              g_tilemap_bg_cache_hits_block,
              g_tilemap_bg_cache_misses_block,
@@ -3430,7 +3430,29 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
              g_tilemap_fg_cache_misses_block > 0
                  ? (double)g_tilemap_fg_miss_total_ns_block / 1e6 / (double)g_tilemap_fg_cache_misses_block
                  : 0.0,
-             _stationary_frac);
+             _stationary_frac,
+             // DOS-PORT (patch 0325): emit the RAW COUNTS beside the ratio.
+             //
+             // stationary_frac is a within-block ratio, and the block
+             // boundary is per-100-FLIPS while both counters are per-TICK.
+             // The flip:tick ratio is hardware-dependent, so the number of
+             // ticks a block spans is too -- ~285 on the Gateway, ~10 under
+             // DOSBox-X on the same reel.
+             //
+             // That makes a MEAN OF BLOCK RATIOS incomparable across
+             // machines. The distribution is bimodal (almost every block
+             // exactly 0.00, rare blocks at 1.00), so one fully-stationary
+             // block contributes 1/18 to an 18-block mean and 1/505 to a
+             // 505-block one. The same reel read 0.11 on hardware and 0.004
+             // locally, and neither is wrong -- they are different
+             // statistics wearing the same name.
+             //
+             // Summing these two counts across blocks gives the pooled
+             // stationary fraction, which IS comparable, and which the
+             // tilemap-cache question depends on: the cache breaks even
+             // near a 63% hit rate and hit rate tracks camera stillness.
+             NXE::Diag::g_w237_stationary_frames_block,
+             NXE::Diag::g_w237_total_frames_block);
   }
   // Reset 12 per-block counters regardless of MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR
   // state. The 2 sticky `*_enabled` flags NOT reset here (per contract
